WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.520
- I actually made a virtual
lunch date with someone

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.980
and our times got screwed
up because he's in London.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.500
And anyway, maybe you won't
mind if I just talk with him

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.050
quickly now because I love him,

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.450
and I've been looking forward
to this moment for a while.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:12.550
I think you might know him

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:13.830
if you live on planet Earth.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.310
He was in some movies
like, "Devil Wears Prada"

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:17.300
and "The Hunger Games,"

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.370
many movies.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:21.920
And his new book is called
"Taste My Life Through Food".

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.717
Stanley, are you there?

00:00:23.717 --> 00:00:25.766
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:25.766 --> 00:00:28.349
(upbeat music)

00:00:29.378 --> 00:00:31.407
Stanley Tucci, everybody!

00:00:31.407 --> 00:00:36.000
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.030
Oh my gosh!

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.960
First of all, what kind of art project

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.100
is happening behind you?

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.910
I'm into whatever is behind you.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.020
What is that?

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:46.400
- I'm sitting in my studio

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.600
where I paint and write and things.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.600
And this is part of
what happens in my mind.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.680
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.240
- I know that you've recently underwent

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.690
successful treatment for cancer.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.993
So, God bless and how are you feeling?

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.090
- Thank you so much.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:05.220
Thank you, yes. I feel,

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.053
I feel great.

00:01:06.053 --> 00:01:07.620
I was very lucky.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:11.960
The cancer I had was a very specific kind

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:16.960
and I had incredible
doctors out at Mount Sinai

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:18.673
in New York,

00:01:20.047 --> 00:01:23.178
and the prognosis is great.

00:01:23.178 --> 00:01:24.180
Thank you.
- Well, as a super fan,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.348
I'm so happy to hear that, man.

00:01:26.348 --> 00:01:27.560
(audience applauding)

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.393
You're such a talent.

00:01:28.393 --> 00:01:29.370
I love everything you do, so.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.460
Thank you for keeping our lunch date.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:32.420
So what are we having today?

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:33.973
'Cause this looks delicious.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:35.850
- Spaghetti

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.090
alla Zucchini,

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.860
- Okay.
- alla Nerano.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.640
- Oh.
- So, it's basically

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.210
the simplest thing in the world.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.650
It's spaghetti

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:47.483
with

00:01:48.951 --> 00:01:51.580
sauteed, or sort of fried,

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:52.420
zucchini.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.775
- [Kelly] Love it fried.

00:01:53.775 --> 00:01:56.297
- [Stanley] And parmesana.

00:01:56.297 --> 00:01:58.938
And it's a specialty of,

00:01:58.938 --> 00:02:01.080
from the Amalfi Coast

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:05.340
and it is one of the most
delicious things I've ever had.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.180
- Okay, well, I am pairing it with a glass

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.320
of Goldeneye Anderson Valley

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:10.153
Pinot Noir,
- [Stanley] Oh!

00:02:10.153 --> 00:02:12.250
the go-to wine on "The
Kelly Clarkson Show".

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:13.500
- [Stanley] That is a great choice.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.900
I think a Pinot Noir
- Thank you.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.830
- is a perfect choice for that.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.490
- I think Pinot Noir is a
perfect choice all the time.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:20.860
Okay. (audience laughing)

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:21.693
(Stanley laughing)

00:02:21.693 --> 00:02:23.650
So I'll just have a taste of that.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.130
I don't know how to
eat spaghetti properly.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:26.070
- [Stanley] Yeah.
- I cut it with a fork

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:26.903
and a knife.

00:02:26.903 --> 00:02:28.510
Every Italian hates me across the world,

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:29.393
but whatever.

00:02:31.039 --> 00:02:33.303
- [Stanley] Okay. Action!
- Oh my God!

00:02:33.303 --> 00:02:34.783
That's really good!

00:02:34.783 --> 00:02:36.130
(audience applauding)

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:36.963
- So simple.

00:02:36.963 --> 00:02:39.160
It's like four ingredients.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:39.993
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:43.990
So if we could have those
sent up to my room for lunch,

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.150
that's where I want that.
(Stanley laughing)

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.230
Yep. That's really good, man.
- Yeah.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.560
- True, speaking of cooking,

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.880
is it true that you actually

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.510
cooked with Meryl Streep in her apartment

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.924
while making "Julie and Julia?"

00:02:54.924 --> 00:02:56.272
- We did.

00:02:56.272 --> 00:02:57.900
We cooked together

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.400
When we were about to start the film,

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.473
I asked her if,

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:04.510
we could cook together.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.580
We had both finished shooting films prior,

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:11.017
and I knew she was busy
and tired, but I said,

00:03:11.017 --> 00:03:15.650
"Not to be too method-y, but
could we just cook together?"

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.770
And we did and we had a great time.

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:20.210
We cooked one of Julia's recipes.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:22.290
We cooked a Blanquette de Veau,

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:25.400
which is a sort of creamy veal dish,

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.030
and it ended up being delicious.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.500
However, it was, we were too slow,

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.560
and we thought we were going
to serve dinner at eight,

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:33.952
we served it at 10.

00:03:33.952 --> 00:03:35.483
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:35.483 --> 00:03:37.450
- This is my problem with cooking, okay.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.810
I can actually cook, but it
takes me like three hours

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.470
to do what it takes someone
like 30 minutes to 45 minutes.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:44.310
I'm so slow 'cause I get nervous

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:46.000
and I triple check everything.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.440
But that's like quite a recipe
- [Stanley] Yeah.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:48.273
- to like,

00:03:48.273 --> 00:03:50.190
be like, "Let's our first
time cooking together...",

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:51.232
you just jumped right into like

00:03:51.232 --> 00:03:53.460
(laughing) a really hard recipe.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.293
That's amazing!

00:03:54.293 --> 00:03:56.330
- Yeah, (laughing) we did. And she,

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:00.040
she had made a Tarte Tatin based on

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.900
Julia's recipe that
was actually delicious.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.500
- Wow! (audience giggling)

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.080
Well, it seemed that you
became even more famous,

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.520
if that's possible,

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.320
for making a drink during lockdown.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.743
So what happened?

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:15.260
- Oh yes. Oh, there I am.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:16.400
That's terrifying.
(audience laughing)

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.340
I made a drink.
- It's not terrifying,

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:19.890
it's sexy!

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.051
Yes!

00:04:21.051 --> 00:04:21.884
- Is it?
- Making a drink

00:04:21.884 --> 00:04:22.717
in all that black!

00:04:22.717 --> 00:04:24.103
Get it! Get it, Stanley!

00:04:24.103 --> 00:04:24.936
(audience cheering, applauding)

00:04:24.936 --> 00:04:26.733
(Kelly giggling)

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:27.566
- Okay.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:30.612
Well, thank you.

00:04:30.612 --> 00:04:32.623
(Kelly giggling)
I don't know to respond.

00:04:32.623 --> 00:04:33.610
(Stanley chuckling)

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:36.697
Yes, my wife Felicity asked me, she said,

00:04:36.697 --> 00:04:38.290
"Would you make a drink for Curtis Brown?"

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:41.501
Which is the agency she
works, oh, there she is!

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:42.807
- Yeah!
- She said,

00:04:42.807 --> 00:04:45.370
"Will you make a drink for the agency,

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:47.470
just a sort of in-house thing,

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:50.380
just to cheer people up
during the first lockdown?"

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.207
And I did. And then she said,

00:04:52.207 --> 00:04:54.860
"Oh, well, let's put it on
the Instagram," you know,

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:58.023
which at the time had seven followers.

00:04:58.023 --> 00:05:00.910
(Kelly laughing)

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:04.037
It's taken over my life
and I'm glad of it.

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:06.885
- It looked like a good drink, that's why.

00:05:06.885 --> 00:05:08.610
Well, tell us about your new book.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:10.414
It's called "Taste My Life Through

00:05:10.414 --> 00:05:11.247
(stammering) Food".

00:05:11.247 --> 00:05:12.415
I can't talk today.

00:05:12.415 --> 00:05:13.400
(audience and Kelly giggling)

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.648
- No, that's okay.

00:05:14.648 --> 00:05:16.327
That's, you know, Pinot Noir.

00:05:16.327 --> 00:05:17.790
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:18.967
- Here, here.

00:05:18.967 --> 00:05:22.180
- I, yes, so I wrote this
book during lockdown.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:25.450
I had written a cookbook
before with Felicity

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:28.040
and helped sort of curate one

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.840
that my parents had done many years ago.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:31.690
But this is,

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:35.500
this is sort of literally
what the title is,

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.240
which is my life through food.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:40.170
Because I realized that, at now,

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:43.500
at the age of 60, that my,

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.120
that everything that I seem to take in,

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:49.774
I take in either visually
or through my mouth.

00:05:49.774 --> 00:05:52.400
(Kelly giggling)
And I experience the world

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.257
almost mostly through my mouth,

00:05:56.257 --> 00:05:57.465
which sounds gross.

00:05:57.465 --> 00:05:59.470
(audience laughing)
- It sounds like a really

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:00.535
naughty novel.

00:06:00.535 --> 00:06:02.396
(audience and Kelly laughing)

00:06:02.396 --> 00:06:05.560
- Yeah, I know. But Kelly, it's about,

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:09.183
that food is connected to every single,

00:06:11.358 --> 00:06:13.410
part of my life.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:18.070
It all revolves around
the most important aspect,

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:19.661
almost is,

00:06:19.661 --> 00:06:21.460
what I eat,

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.070
and

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.180
how I share that with people.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.580
- That's my favorite
part is how you share it.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:27.650
That's what I love about a dinner,

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.660
everybody getting together
and it's always around food,

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:32.030
whether it's like a lunch
thing or a dinner party.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.240
I love, that's my favorite thing,

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.440
is the mingling and all the people.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:36.864
So that's, I love food as well.

00:06:36.864 --> 00:06:37.697
(audience and Kelly giggling)

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:39.090
- It's the best way to make friends.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:40.400
And it's the best way,

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.993
it's the best way to,

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.850
to find a common ground, I think.

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:46.910
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.980
(audience applauding)
Especially if it's great food.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.070
Well, this was delicious, and I, no joke,

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.080
will be eating it for lunch.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.970
Thank you. It was great to see you!

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.737
I love your art studio.

00:06:55.737 --> 00:06:57.856
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:06:57.856 --> 00:06:59.563
Take care, and thanks
for the zucchini pasta!

